{
  "below": [
    {"name": "crates", "role": "Rust workspace crates: the runtime, the HTTP door, the ABI mirrors and the omega FFI wrappers"},
    {"name": "doctrine", "role": "Project doctrine and design records"},
    {"name": "docs", "role": "Documentation, ADRs and operator guides"},
    {"name": "om", "role": "First-party seeded Omega (.om) replacements and checks, each with a pinned omc"},
    {"name": "scripts", "role": "Build, release and check scripts"},
    {"name": "skills", "role": "Agent skills shipped with the repository"},
    {"name": "tests", "role": "Repository-level gates; tests/gates/run.sh is the single local gate entry point"},
    {"name": "tools", "role": "Developer tools, including the local CI runner"}
  ],
  "extensions": {
    "generated_policy": "on-demand"
  },
  "invariants": [
    "No crumb commits an extensions.generated block; generated data is derived on demand. crumb verify fails on a committed generated block or on a crumb that is not a JSON object, and checks nothing else about which fields a crumb holds. The hosted AIEN Checks job also runs crumb verify . with the pinned tool, but that job is advisory and gates no merge. Check: tests/gates/run.sh crumb-verify (gate CRUMB-VERIFY)"
  ],
  "name": "aien-sovereign-core",
  "purpose": "AIEN Sovereign Core: the Rust host runtime, the loopback OpenAI-compatible HTTP door (aien-serve-http) and the FFI to the omega GPU kernels",
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
